================================================================================
PHASE 5: ORDER MANAGEMENT (FEATURE_ROADMAP Phase 4)
================================================================================
Status: ✅ CORE DONE — polish remaining

Schema + JPA:
  orders       → OrderEntity    (order_number, status, payment_status, total_amount, address FKs)
  order_items  → OrderItemEntity (quantity, price snapshot)

Flow (implemented):
  Add Product → Add To Cart → Checkout → Create Order → Reduce Inventory → Clear Cart Items

Implemented:
  [x] OrderEntity, OrderItemEntity
  [x] OrderStatus, PaymentStatus enums
  [x] IOrderRepository, IOrderItemRepository
  [x] OrderService.placeOrder (CheckoutRequestDto) with @Transactional
  [x] OrderController — checkout, list, detail, cancel
  [x] OrderNotFoundException, InvalidOrderStateException + handlers
  [x] EmptyCartException, AddressNotBelongsToUserException, InactiveUserException

Endpoints (live):
  POST   /orders/checkout
  GET    /orders                     (header: user_id)
  GET    /orders/{orderId}             (header: user_id)
  PATCH  /orders/{orderId}/cancel      (header: user_id)

Checkout business rules (@Transactional) — all implemented:
  1. Validate cart not empty
  2. Validate shipping/billing address belongs to user
  3. Re-check stock for every cart item
  4. Create orders row; create order_items with price snapshot
  5. Decrement stock_quantity; clear cart items
  6. Roll back on any failure

Remaining polish:
  [ ] Frontend checkout / order history UI
  [ ] OrderService unit + integration tests
  [ ] Safer order_number generation under concurrency
  [ ] Resolve userId from JWT (after Auth phase)
  [ ] Optional JPA @OneToMany / @ManyToOne on order entities

Learn (completed):
- @Transactional, ACID, Rollback, Concurrency

